 In a narrow sense, taste is commonly confused with aesthetics. This is not false, except that aesthetics itself is nowadays also a commonly misunderstood concept. Aesthetic is often used interchangeably with “pretty”.</p>

<p>In an organization, the responsibility of taste cannot be outsourced or borne by a single person (think Apple under Steve Jobs: even then, he wasn’t the only person with taste, in fact, the decision making process is a matter of escalating taste. Every layer of executive was expected to use their taste in evaluating a product). Cultivating good taste is the responsibility of every decision maker.</p>
